---
import Newsletter from '../../../components/islands/Newsletter.island.astro';
import SimplePage from '../../../components/content/SimplePage.astro';
import { getCtaLinks } from '../../../lib/cms.ts';
const { healthCheckUrl } = await getCtaLinks();

// Official Home Affairs global processing-times tool — the authoritative source.
const IMMI_TIMES =
  'https://immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-processing-times/global-visa-processing-times';
---

<SimplePage
  title="Visa Processing Times"
  description="How to check current Australian visa processing times, why they change, and how we keep your matter moving — from a Registered Migration Agent in Perth."
  eyebrow="Knowledge Centre"
  lead="Processing times change often. Here's how to check the current position — and how we keep your matter moving."
  cta={{ href: healthCheckUrl, label: 'Check your position' }}
  disclaimer={true}
>
  <p>
    Australian visa processing times vary by subclass, by your individual circumstances, and by the
    Department of Home Affairs' current workloads — and they are updated regularly. Because of that,
    the most reliable figure is always the current published one.
  </p>
  <p>The Department publishes indicative global processing times for each visa, updated monthly:</p>
  <p>
    <a href={IMMI_TIMES} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Home Affairs — global visa processing times →</a
    >
  </p>
  <h2>How we keep your matter moving</h2>
  <p>
    Processing time is not something any agent controls — but a well-prepared, complete application
    avoids the requests for more information that add weeks or months. For every matter we prepare
    the evidence carefully, respond to any departmental request promptly, and track your deadlines,
    so nothing stalls that we can prevent.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you engage us, we confirm the processing time currently published for your pathway and set
    honest expectations for your circumstances. Times can change while an application is on foot; we
    keep you informed through to the decision.
  </p>
  <div style="margin-block-start: var(--space-6);"><Newsletter /></div>
</SimplePage>
